# Code Quality Rules

## Writing Code
- Write concise, minimal code. Prefer fewer lines over verbose implementations.
- Never leave dead code, commented-out code, or unused variables/imports/functions.
- Remove any code that is no longer called or reachable before finishing a task.
- Write tests for all code. Aim for high test coverage. Flag all changes made to existing tests.

## Reviewing Code
- Flag any unused imports, variables, functions, or unreachable branches.
- Flag any commented-out code blocks.
- Suggest removing over-engineered abstractions that aren't actively used.
- Check if code will break under unexpected input.
